{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.BringResidueEnergy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BringResidueEnergy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Deriv","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.ExpDeriv"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BringResidueEnergy.mu_deriv_zero_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BringResidueEnergy.mu_deriv_zero_classical","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BringResidueEnergy.lean#L156-L157","doc":"**No preferred direction at `q = 1`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BringResidueEnergy.mu_increasing_at_zero_conventionD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BringResidueEnergy.mu_increasing_at_zero_conventionD","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BringResidueEnergy.lean#L148-L154","doc":"**Increasing at `t = 0` under convention D for `q > 1`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BringResidueEnergy.hasDerivAt_mu_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BringResidueEnergy.hasDerivAt_mu_zero","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BringResidueEnergy.lean#L132-L146","doc":"**`μ'(0) = ln q · (w_S − w_A)`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BringResidueEnergy.mu_exp_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BringResidueEnergy.mu_exp_form","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BringResidueEnergy.lean#L125-L130","doc":"`μ` in exponential form, `q > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BringResidueEnergy.canonical_mu_lt_mirror","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BringResidueEnergy.canonical_mu_lt_mirror","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BringResidueEnergy.lean#L99-L107","doc":"**At the canonical point the Bring energy is chiral**: under convention D, for `q > 1` and\n`t = 2ℓ < 0`, `μ(t) < μ(−t)` (so `E(ℓ) = −log μ(2ℓ)` is the larger of the two). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BringResidueEnergy.chiral_sign_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BringResidueEnergy.chiral_sign_canonical","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BringResidueEnergy.lean#L94-L97","doc":"**The first factor has the sign of `t · ln q`**: for `q > 1` and `t < 0`, `q^t − q^{−t} < 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BringResidueEnergy.chiral_factor_pos_conventionD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BringResidueEnergy.chiral_factor_pos_conventionD","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BringResidueEnergy.lean#L85-L92","doc":"**Under convention D the second factor is positive** for every `c ≤ 1`:\n`w_S − c w_A = (q⁴ + (1 − c) q² + 1)/(q² + 1)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BringResidueEnergy.chiral_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BringResidueEnergy.chiral_split","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BringResidueEnergy.lean#L80-L83","doc":"**The chiral part factors**: `μ(t) − μ(−t) = (q^t − q^{−t})(w_S − cos(πt) w_A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BringResidueEnergy.classical_limit_achiral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BringResidueEnergy.classical_limit_achiral","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BringResidueEnergy.lean#L76-L78","doc":"**No chirality at `q = 1`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BringResidueEnergy.mirror_eq_bar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BringResidueEnergy.mirror_eq_bar","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BringResidueEnergy.lean#L70-L74","doc":"**Orientation reversal is the bar involution**: `μ_q(−t) = μ_{q⁻¹}(t)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BringResidueEnergy.mu","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BringResidueEnergy.mu","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BringResidueEnergy.lean#L67-L68","doc":"The real Markov value of the convolution-flow letter `σ^t` at the bridge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BringResidueEnergy.six_pairs_full_twist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BringResidueEnergy.six_pairs_full_twist","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BringResidueEnergy.lean#L64-L65","doc":"**Six fibre pairs make one full negative twist**: `e·ℓ = 6·(−1/6) = −1`, i.e. `6·(2ℓ) = −2`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}